  "title": {
    "rendered": "Pro Bono Program Summer 2027 Clerkship"
  },
  "content": {
    "rendered": "<p>ALDF&#8217;s Pro Bono Program works to expand the practice and understanding of animal law in the legal community, connecting law firms, bar associations, and practitioners with animal protection work.</p>\n<h3>What You&#8217;ll Do</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Research law firms, bar associations, CLEs, and opportunities in animal law</li>\n<li>Work on housing/animal custody issues, dangerous dog designations, breed-specific restrictions</li>\n<li>Research tort law matters, negligence issues, and questions around animals as legal property</li>\n<li>Participate in networking and engagement activities</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Requirements</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Current 2L (or part-time equivalent) or LLM student at an ABA-accredited law school</li>\n<li>Eligibility to work in the United States</li>\n<li>Superior legal research and writing skills</li>\n<li>Sincere interest in animal protection; familiarity with animal law preferred</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>How to Apply</h3>\n<p>Apply via Paylocity. Required: resume, cover letter, references, law school transcript, and writing sample. <strong>Deadline: 20 November 2026.</strong></p>\n",
    "protected": false
  },
  "excerpt": {
    "rendered": "<p>10-week summer clerkship in ALDF&#8217;s Pro Bono Program. Researches law firms and bar associations; works on housing/animal custody issues, breed-specific restrictions, tort law, and expanding animal law practice.</p>\n",
    "protected": false
  },
